# THE BUILD CONTEXT IS UPLOADED IN FULL, SO THIS FILE IS A COST CONTROL.
#
# The repo is 1.7 GB. Without this, every `gcloud run deploy` would ship all
# of it to Cloud Build before the first instruction runs — most of it raw
# Overture snapshots that the image does not contain and must never contain.
# With it, the context is ~35 MB: the Go source, the derived tables, and the
# built SPA.

# 429 MB of immutable source snapshots. The image carries data/derived only.
data/raw/

# Rebuilt by `npm ci` in CI and not used by the runtime image at all.
web/node_modules/
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The frozen study. Provenance for the rules, not an input to the binary.
research/

# Local state, none of it reproducible or wanted in an image.
.git/
.dev-logs/
.dev-certs/
.claude/
docs/

# Host-built artefacts. The image builds its own binary from source, and a
# host binary here would be the wrong architecture as often as not.
api/thirdeye-api
api/api

# Pipeline sources: the image serves precomputed tables, it does not build them.
pipeline/
